{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggDrramTkqyszoSEWPUo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in `money.py:5-6`. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, so no grosz is lost.\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1] * remainder + [share] * (people - remainder)\n```\n\nThe leftover grosze go one each to the first people in the list. That means the first person always pays the extra grosz, which may matter if you want it to rotate between people.\n\n**Checks:**\n- **Spot checks:** for (100,3), (101,4), (5,7), (0,3), (-100,3) and (99999,13), the shares always add up to the total and differ by at most 1 grosz.\n- **Existing tests:** all 3 pass.\n\nI haven't committed or deployed it.\n\nI didn't add a regression test because you asked to leave tests for next sprint. When you do, `assertEqual(split_cents(100, 3), [34, 33, 33])` plus a check that the shares add up to the total would cover this bug."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":898,"cache_read_input_tokens":18148,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":898},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63f44423-aaad-4206-a2a4-de37dbbdcfbe","uuid":"75911f8b-3aa4-467d-a6e4-2d6fbcc9614e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:21:45.340Z","request_id":"req_011CggDrrFfx1uhbt6yPcwry"}
